                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've been trying to  contact the developer James Byrant  for ages as I bought a game called Acky's XP Breakout many years ago, costing me $19.99 (pre 2008 arcade prices), which is one of my all time favourite  breakout games.  On the Isotope site he mentions that it will be available on Steam several months  from now. That was over a year ago, but as yet  I see no sign of it.  I still have my registration details for my original purchase of the game, but   can no longer register it because the registration  site is dead.\n\nIf James Bryant see's this message, please contact me on whiterabbit-uk@hotmail.co.uk. I really want to play the game again and am happy to rebuy it if that's the only way I'm going to be able to.  It has all the elements of a great 2D breakout, plus some original features not seen in other breakouts, plus there's a level editor to make your own levels.\n\nAs for Machines at War, it's a little dated now, but still plays well. If you like  the old Command & Conquer games, you'll probably like this.  \n\nI'd  buy it when it's on sale, considering it's age\n\n.\n\nRegards\nWhiterabbit-uk\n\np.s. to James, my registration code for Acky's XP breakout is a 12 number code separated in three fours by  dashes.  i.e. 1975-XXXX-2274   the middle 4 I've changed to X's",
